## Q11. Use EarlyStopping and ModelCheckpoint

**Program:**
```python
import tensorflow as tf
import numpy as np

np.random.seed(42)
tf.random.set_seed(42)

x = np.arange(100, dtype="float32").reshape(-1, 1) / 100
y = 2 * x + 1

model = tf.keras.Sequential([
    tf.keras.Input(shape=(1,)),
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(16, activation="relu"),
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(1)
])

model.compile(optimizer="adam", loss="mse")

callbacks = [
    tf.keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(
        monitor="val_loss", patience=5,
        restore_best_weights=True
    ),
    tf.keras.callbacks.ModelCheckpoint(
        "best_model.keras",
        monitor="val_loss",
        save_best_only=True
    )
]

history = model.fit(
    x, y, epochs=50, batch_size=16,
    validation_split=0.2, callbacks=callbacks,
    verbose=0
)

print("Training completed.")
print("Epochs executed:", len(history.history["loss"]))
print("Best model saved as best_model.keras")
```

