## Q12. Use Dropout to Reduce Overfitting

**Program:**
```python
import tensorflow as tf
import numpy as np

np.random.seed(42)
tf.random.set_seed(42)

x = np.random.rand(200, 10).astype("float32")
y = (x.sum(axis=1) > 5).astype("float32")

model = tf.keras.Sequential([
    tf.keras.Input(shape=(10,)),
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(64, activation="relu"),
    tf.keras.layers.Dropout(0.5),
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(32, activation="relu"),
    tf.keras.layers.Dropout(0.3),
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(1, activation="sigmoid")
])

model.compile(optimizer="adam",
              loss="binary_crossentropy",
              metrics=["accuracy"])

history = model.fit(
    x, y, epochs=20, batch_size=16,
    validation_split=0.2, verbose=0
)

print("Training accuracy:",
      round(history.history["accuracy"][-1], 4))
print("Validation accuracy:",
      round(history.history["val_accuracy"][-1], 4))
print("Dropout helps reduce overfitting.")
```

**Output:**
```text
Training accuracy: A numerical value
Validation accuracy: A numerical value
Dropout helps reduce overfitting.
```

**Explanation:** Dropout training ke dauran kuch neurons ko randomly deactivate karta hai. Isse model training data par excessively dependent hone se bach sakta hai. Lekin dropout overfitting ko eliminate karne ki guarantee nahi deta.

## Q13. Functional API for Multiple Inputs and Outputs

**Program:**
```python
import tensorflow as tf
import numpy as np

input1 = tf.keras.Input(shape=(2,), name="input_one")
input2 = tf.keras.Input(shape=(2,), name="input_two")

combined = tf.keras.layers.Concatenate()([input1, input2])
hidden = tf.keras.layers.Dense(8, activation="relu")(combined)

output1 = tf.keras.layers.Dense(1, name="output_one")(hidden)
output2 = tf.keras.layers.Dense(1, activation="sigmoid",
                               name="output_two")(hidden)

model = tf.keras.Model(
    inputs=[input1, input2],
    outputs=[output1, output2]
)

model.compile(
    optimizer="adam",
    loss={"output_one": "mse",
          "output_two": "binary_crossentropy"}
)

a = np.random.rand(20, 2).astype("float32")
b = np.random.rand(20, 2).astype("float32")
y1 = np.random.rand(20, 1).astype("float32")
y2 = np.random.randint(0, 2, (20, 1)).astype("float32")

model.fit(
    {"input_one": a, "input_two": b},
    {"output_one": y1, "output_two": y2},
    epochs=5, verbose=0
)

result = model.predict(
    {"input_one": a[:1], "input_two": b[:1]},
    verbose=0
)

print("Output one:", result[0])
print("Output two:", result[1])
```

**Output:**
